* /**
*  * @file GIT.FILECLASS
*  * @version 1.0
*  */
* GIT.FILECLASS(FILE, CTL) — the LIVE file's class, in the open interchange
* spelling: "DIR", or "hash <modulo> STATIC|DYNAMIC", or a bare "hash" when the
* platform has no size to report.
*
* ONE COPY.  This was written out three times — in GIT.ADD, in GIT.STATUS, and
* nearly a fourth in GIT.ATTR — and three copies of a rule is how the sticky
* control came to be applied on two staging paths out of three (540c066).  The
* drift check in particular has to ask the question the SAME way `add` asks it,
* or a file would read as diverged the moment the two copies disagreed.
      SUBROUTINE GIT.FILECLASS(FILE, CTL)
      $INCLUDE BP.INC PLATFORM.H
      CTL = "hash"
      $IFNDEF MVX
*     FILEINFO key 3 is the type and key 5 the modulus.  A directory file has no
*     modulus, which is what separates it from a hashed one.
      OPEN FILE TO FCVAR THEN
         FTY = FILEINFO(FCVAR, 3) ; MODL = FILEINFO(FCVAR, 5)
         IF MODL <= 0 THEN
            CTL = "DIR"
         END ELSE
            IF FTY = 2 THEN DS = "STATIC" ELSE DS = "DYNAMIC"
            CTL = "hash " : MODL : " " : DS
         END
      END
      $ENDIF
      $IFDEF MVX
*     MVX HAS NO FILEINFO, and needs none: a file's live description IS its
*     dictionary's own %FILE% record — `FILE` and the driver — which is what the
*     account opens it by.  It says which KIND of file this is and nothing about
*     size, because an LMDB-backed file has no modulo to report.
      OPEN "DICT", FILE TO FCDV THEN
         FCREC = ""
         READ FCREC FROM FCDV, "%FILE%" THEN
            IF OCONV(FCREC<1, 2>, "MCL") = "dir" THEN CTL = "DIR"
         END
      END
      $ENDIF
      RETURN
      END
